IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il40-nouns`
IMPORT `il40-days`

-- TESTS for sections 5 to 10.  Hand rules: the text names Independence Day (national holiday), the two memorial days, the Sabbath and the festivals of Israel (days of rest),
-- the Hebrew and the Gregorian calendars; a day or a calendar it does not name is NOTHING (the lists are not closed).  The right in s 10 is given to those who are not Jews.

§ `Tests: sections 5 to 10`

#ASSERT `the section that puts on the State the duty` `to be open to Jewish immigration and to the ingathering of exiles` EQUALS "s 5"
#ASSERT `the section that puts on the State the duty` `to endeavour to secure the safety of Jews and of citizens in distress or captivity because of their Jewishness or citizenship` EQUALS "s 6(a)"
#ASSERT `the section that puts on the State the duty` `to act in the Diaspora to preserve the bond between the State and Jews` EQUALS "s 6(b)"
#ASSERT `the section that puts on the State the duty` `to act to preserve the cultural, historical and religious heritage of the Jewish people among Diaspora Jewry` EQUALS "s 6(c)"
#ASSERT `the section that puts on the State the duty` `to act to encourage and promote the establishment and consolidation of Jewish settlement` EQUALS "s 7"

#ASSERT `s 6(a) puts on the State the duty to endeavour to secure the safety of the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) puts on the State the duty to endeavour to secure the safety of the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) puts on the State the duty to endeavour to secure the safety of the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(a) puts on the State the duty to endeavour to secure the safety of the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(a) puts on the State the duty to endeavour to secure the safety of the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 8 makes the calendar an official calendar of the State` `the Hebrew calendar` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8 makes the calendar an official calendar of the State` `the Gregorian calendar` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8 makes the calendar an official calendar of the State` `another calendar` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `the standing s 9 gives to` `Independence Day` EQUALS JUST `the official national holiday of the State`
#ASSERT `the standing s 9 gives to` `Memorial Day for the fallen of Israel's wars` EQUALS JUST `an official memorial day of the State`
#ASSERT `the standing s 9 gives to` `Holocaust and Heroism Remembrance Day` EQUALS JUST `an official memorial day of the State`
#ASSERT `the standing s 9 gives to` `the Sabbath` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the standing s 9 gives to` `another day` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 10 makes the day one of the fixed days of rest of the State` `the Sabbath` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10 makes the day one of the fixed days of rest of the State` `a festival of Israel` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10 makes the day one of the fixed days of rest of the State` `Independence Day` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10 makes the day one of the fixed days of rest of the State` `another day` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10 gives the person the right to keep the days of rest on their own Sabbath and festivals` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10 gives the person the right to keep the days of rest on their own Sabbath and festivals` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
